# RoT DTD GOAL -- line endings are a correctness property here, not a style one.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Every archive this project shipped measured ZERO
# carriage returns, and the fourth reviewer still received 77 CRLF lines across
# 7 files. The tree was clean; the TRANSIT was not. A shell script with CRLF
# fails in ways that read as nonsense -- `bash\r: no such file`, a `then\r`
# that never matches -- and the author's platform is the one that introduces
# them silently. So the rule is pinned in the repository, where it survives a
# clone onto a machine configured with core.autocrlf=true.
#
# Effect: git stores LF, and checks out LF, on every platform, forever.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.zip  binary
*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary

# Shell and Lean must be LF even if a future rule tries to be clever.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.lean  text eol=lf
*.tsv   text eol=lf
*.dtd   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
